A maintainer on the project nickderobertis/crozier (unknown) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:

Issue #84: Recursive schemas generate broken code: self-referential model self-imports (circular); recursive union stack-overflows

Recursive schemas generate broken code — a self-referential model emits an
import of its own name (circular import at load), and a recursive discriminated
union crashes the generator with a stack overflow. Both are common shapes
(trees, nested/recursive predicates), and both slip past `compileall` — the
first because a self-import is syntactically valid, the second because there's
no output to check.

Environment: `crozier 0.0.23`.

## Case A — self-referential model → self-import → circular import

Minimal spec `tree.json` (a node that contains a list of itself):

```json
{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": { "title": "Widget API", "version": "1.0.0" },
  "paths": {
    "/tree": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "putTree",
        "requestBody": { "content": { "application/json": {
          "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TreeNode" } } } },
        "responses": { "200": { "description": "OK" } }
      }
    }
  },
  "components": { "schemas": {
    "TreeNode": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "value": { "type": "string" },
        "children": { "type": "array", "items": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TreeNode" } }
      }
    }
  } }
}
```

Generates `src/widget_api/types/tree_node.py` whose **first import is of its own
name**:

```python
from .tree_node import TreeNode   # <-- module imports itself
```

`compileall` passes, but any real import fails:

```
>>> from widget_api import TreeNode
ImportError: cannot import name 'TreeNode' from partially initialized module
'widget_api.types.tree_node' (most likely due to a circular import)
```

The line is dead wrong — a module never needs to import a name it defines. The
recursive field annotation should be a forward reference (the file already has
`from __future__ import annotations`, so `children: typing.List["TreeNode"]`
needs no import at all).

## Case B — recursive discriminated union → stack overflow (generator crash)

Minimal spec `recursive_union.json` (a `oneOf` whose variant references the
union recursively):

```json
{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": { "title": "Widget API", "version": "1.0.0" },
  "paths": {
    "/pred": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "putPred",
        "requestBody": { "content": { "application/json": {
          "schema": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Node" } } } },
        "responses": { "200": { "description": "OK" } }
      }
    }
  },
  "components": { "schemas": {
    "Node": {
      "oneOf": [
        { "type": "object", "title": "AndNode", "required": ["kind", "children"],
          "properties": { "kind": { "type": "string", "enum": ["and"] },
            "children": { "type": "array", "items": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Node" } } } },
        { "type": "object", "title": "LeafNode", "required": ["kind", "name"],
          "properties": { "kind": { "type": "string", "enum": ["leaf"] },
            "name": { "type": "string" } } }
      ],
      "discriminator": { "propertyName": "kind" }
    }
  } }
}
```

`crozier generate` aborts:

```
thread 'main' has overflowed its stack
fatal runtime error: stack overflow, aborting
```

The generator recurses into `Node` → `AndNode.children` → `Node` → … without a
visited-set / cycle guard. (A recursive union with named `$ref` variants + a
discriminator mapping does emit output, but with the Case-A self-import on the
union alias module — so both recursion shapes need the same cycle-aware fix.)

## Impact

Both shapes are ordinary — self-referential trees and recursive rule/predicate
unions are common in real specs. Any generated SDK that touches such a type is
either uncompilable to import (Case A) or ungenerable at all (Case B).

## Suggested fix

- Never emit `from .<mod> import <Name>` for the name the module itself defines;
  rely on `from __future__ import annotations` + string forward refs for
  self/mutually-recursive references.
- Add a visited-set cycle guard to the schema-walk so recursive `oneOf`/`$ref`
  graphs terminate instead of overflowing the stack.


